  "notes": "The stopped-rotor machine (PLAN §0, Phase 5): a tip-prop rotor lifts it like the tipjet; slide the mode and the tip props die, the park controller brakes the head and indexes the blades spanwise, and the same two blades are now the WING - collec\n\nEXPORT NOTES — contact spring numbers are Flightline-typical, not converted — the two contact models differ. drag CdA per axis estimated from the drag parts (x, 2x, 3x). head speed om0 57 rad/s: set by what the tip propellers can still pull at, not by the head — three quarters of their pitch speed at the mounting radius. Whirligig flies this head faster; Flightline's linear propeller model cannot drive it that fast. tip drive: 2 props at 0.675 m, Tmax estimated 15.6 N each, zero-thrust speed 51.28 m/s, pod drag kD 0.00055 from a 46 mm nacelle. 1 forward prop(s) exported as thrusters (Tmax estimated); differential yaw where they sit off-centre. Tmin 0: these propellers only pull forward, so the hover holds its nose with one of the pair idle and the other against the torque, and it hovers slightly nose-up because of it. no yaw device in the source; a 1.17 N·m mast motor added so the pedal works — Flightline's own tip-drive yaws the same way.",
